## O4. webcodecs-engine — the keystone  [P1, big; CONTINUES ee/webcodecs-capture-2 (on origin, behind main — rebase first)]
Why: the pixel path (MediaRecorder + <video> + main-thread 2D canvas) forces 4–6 redundant decodes
during capture, fixed-tick redraws of static frames, no keyframe control, ±45 ms epoch jitter, and the
1080p capture ceiling.
Step 1 DONE 2026-08-23 (×10 runs, evidence in DECISIONS): the residual is the INSTRUMENT.
Measured: an exact +18.00 ms detection bias (half a 30 fps frame + half a 128-sample envelope window;
predicted 18.00, measured 18.00 sd 0.00, 10/10) plus a video reference delay of 13.22 ms that the
oracle had always assumed to be zero while measuring the audio side (new probeFlashArrivals). CI's
metric read 31.55 ms (sd 7.86) over 10 runs; the same exports fully referenced read 62.77 ms (sd 8.73).
So the true offset is ~45–63 ms, every past sync number is ~31 ms optimistic, and the ≤10 ms gate is
NOT measurable here: 1σ is ~8–9 ms, so 10/10 under 10 ms would fail on noise even with a perfect engine.
Step 1b DONE 2026-08-23 (O4b): CI now gates the SYMMETRIC metric (both rig references measured, both
detection biases removed) at ≤90 ms — 5/5 cold PASS at 40.5-66.2 ms. Production anchor now subtracts
the platform-reported input latency (loopback: the anchor placed impulses +128.7 ms late, sd 0.70; the
audio clock agreed within 1.1 ms, so the delay is signal-path, not messaging). Instrument noise floor is
~8-9 ms 1σ — the honest limit for any future band.
STEP 2 (the engine, still to do): MediaStreamTrackProcessor → worker compositor (OffscreenCanvas,
WebGPU→WebGL→2D) → VideoEncoder (prefer-hardware, realtime, keyframe ≤2 s) → fMP4 → positioned OPFS
writer. Frame-driven draw, preview renders the compositor's own output, MediaRecorder stays as the
watchdog fallback, crash-salvage must recover the fMP4 mid-write. THIS is where O3a's rejected hardware
encode returns — we own the muxer, so bytes land on disk as they are produced.
GOAL FOR THE GATE: bring the symmetric sync metric to ≤20 ms and re-tighten the band.
Harness: `npm run exp -- o4step1`, `npm run exp -- audiolat`.
Step 2: MediaStreamTrackProcessor → VideoFrames transferred to a WORKER compositor (OffscreenCanvas;
WebGPU importExternalTexture preferred, WebGL then 2D fallback) → VideoEncoder (prefer-hardware,
realtime, keyframe cadence ≤2 s — the smart-cut prerequisite) → fMP4 mux → positioned durable OPFS
writer. Frame-driven draw (encode on frame arrival, ~1 fps keep-alive when static), not a fixed 30 Hz
tick. The on-screen recording preview renders the compositor's own output — zero extra <video>
decodes. SourceLiveness feeds from frame arrivals (worklet tick remains the clock). Raw channel
capture may also move to VideoEncoder on Chromium in the same worker — optional, evidence decides.
Constraints: MediaRecorder path stays as capability/watchdog fallback (weak machine degrades, proven);
crash-salvage must recover the fMP4 composite mid-write (ABSORBS v1 task 4 — composite salvage becomes
free); measured-audio pipeline untouched; instant export contract unchanged.
